# The load split: with the carriage and head (12 kg) near Y1's rail, Y1
# carries more of the bridge's acceleration than Y2 (current), and the
# other way round near Y2; in the middle both share it. With the drives'
# exact command feedforward and unbiased velocity observer (y.conf) the
# two loops hold the bridge square (a few urad) wherever the load is.
@todo master's F3 voltage limit (DEBUGNOTES 2026-10-26 "Portal: the linear motors run out of bus voltage")
@program portal/portal_sim
@args portal/machine/portal.portal
run 0.05
lcnc 1
run 0.2
move 0.5 50 300
run 0.3
mark
move 0.6 50 700
print max_cur_y1 max_cur_y2 max_rack
move 0.9 950 700
run 0.3
mark
move 0.6 950 300
print max_cur_y1 max_cur_y2 max_rack
move 0.6 500 300
run 0.3
mark
move 0.6 500 700
print max_cur_y1 max_cur_y2 max_rack fault jammed
@expect portal.max_cur_y1[1] > 1.25
@expect portal.max_cur_y2[1] < 1.05
@expect portal.max_cur_y1[2] < 1.05
@expect portal.max_cur_y2[2] > 1.25
@expect portal.max_cur_y1[3] ~ 1.29 4%
@expect portal.max_cur_y2[3] ~ 1.29 4%
@expect max portal.max_rack < 15
@expect portal.fault == 0
@expect portal.jammed == 0
@reject ^ERROR
